k solid walls and a front wall with a central 1.0-wide entrance; passable interior uses actual actor clearance. Reject overlap with solids, actors, reserved sites or world bounds, and require an exterior approach and navigable entrance; reserve the footprint during building without trapping or displacing actors. Navigation, collision, visibility and occupancy use these same shapes. Walking through the entrance uses navigate; rest remains rest, without an extra energy-recovery bonus.\\nThermal dependency: integrate with the existing authoritative temperature/exposure update, not a cosmetic shelter flag. For a living actor whose center is inside the interior, multiply the adverse cold-exposure component by 0.5, leaving baseline ambient temperature, heat exposure and all other physiological terms unchanged. Do not multiply protection from overlapping shelters. If the current updater lacks a separable cold term, refactor it preserving all unsheltered results before activating protection. Show measured sheltered and counterfactual unsheltered cold contributions, not a promise of fixed warming. Protection lasts 160 simulation rounds after completion, then expires; the expired frame remains collidable and visibly uninsulated. Public shelter-maintain schema {target:string}, required, no extra fields: within 0.65 of entrance, reserve and consume 4 owned dry-grass units over 2 stationary rounds costing 1 energy each, with the same cancellation/death rules; completion restores 160 remaining rounds, never adds beyond 160. No healing, food, invulnerability, free rest energy or guaranteed safe temperature.\\nDeclare and validate subscriptions for shelter-build-started, shelter-build-progress, shelter-build-completed, shelter-build-cancelled, shelter-maintenance-started, shelter-maintenance-completed, shelter-maintenance-cancelled, shelter-protection-expired, shelter-exposure-measured and shelter-comfort-qualified. Events carry actor/target IDs, tick, success, actual costs and relevant measured effects. Bind public observations, rendering and personal memory adapters to these events. Dependencies are existing inventory escrow, metabolism/death, shared geometry/navigation, temperature and wellbeing systems; implement missing adapters in this handoff. Version migration initializes an empty shelter registry and no active jobs, preserves existing resources/history/vitals, registers schemas and events before subscribers, and grants no objects, stock or mastery.\",\"experienceReview\":\"Actual relief from cold can plausibly benefit Sol, but construction completion alone is not evidence of relief. Register one thermal-refuge source, deduplicated against any equivalent future comfort source. Emit shelter-comfort-qualified for the occupying actor only after 3 consecutive living, stationary rounds resting or waiting inside an active shelter, with positive measured avoided cold loss each round and a strictly lower existing cold-discomfort penalty than the unsheltered calculation. Require no starvation or health loss during that interval. Award 1 mental wellbeing, cap 1, for 6 rounds; cooldown 12 rounds from award, repeat awards allowed under the same conditions, refresh rather than stack. Reset qualification on exit, death, expired protection or failed conditions. Participants are actual occupants individually, not the builder or owner by proxy. Physical wellbeing continues to derive independently from actual hunger, health, fatigue and temperature; requesting, learning, labels and merely owning or seeing the shelter award nothing.\",\"visualReview\":\"Render the actual rotated frame, packed-grass covering, open entrance and shared collision outline; unfinished construction shows progress without appearing usable. Completed, expired and maintenance states must be visibly distinct. Selecting an observed shelter exposes its recipe, service time, occupancy and measured thermal contribution through shelter-exposure-measured; do not expose hidden objects or claim protection outside its interior. Show comfort feedback only on a qualified personal event. No shelter is rendered as an existing world object until real construction succeeds.\",\"learning\":5}]}","annotations":[],"logprobs":[]}}

